      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`FlashInferAttnBackend._prepare_cuda_graph_metadata` creates a new set of decode (or target-verify)\nwrappers for every capture and stores it in `decode_cuda_graph_metadata[bs]`. Replay\n(`init_forward_metadata_out_graph`) plans only that stored set. The decode runner captures one batch\nsize more than once when it records attention graph variants (`graph_variants.py`) or LoRA / no-LoRA\ngraphs; the earlier graphs then replay kernels bound to wrappers whose plan is never refreshed — stale\nindices / lengths, silently.\n\n## Modifications\n\nReuse the stored wrappers for a batch size if they exist (decode and target-verify). The wrappers are\nbound to the same per-bs buffer slices either way, so sharing them is what the replay path assumes.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- New unit test `test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_flashinfer_graph_variant_wrappers.py`: fails\n  on main (a second capture of bs=4 yields different wrappers), passes with the fix.\n- End to end: a model capturing two decode-graph variants per batch size on FlashInfer gives\n  decode-vs-prefill logprob consistency of 8 / 2,048 top-1 flips (plain-decode level) with the fix.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNone: fewer wrapper objects, same kernels.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] pre-commit\n- [x] regression test (fails before, passes after)\n\n## AI assistance\n\nThis change was developed with AI assistance (Claude Code). The tests and measurements reported here were\nrun by us on our own hardware, and we will follow up on review feedback.\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39202600078](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39202600078)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39202600035](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39202600035)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39202599998](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39202599998)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
